WEBVTT

00:09:26.561 --> 00:09:30.101
just as black women today
started Black Lives Matter.

00:09:30.601 --> 00:09:33.481
JMR: And some of the same
people who fought for

00:09:33.505 --> 00:09:35.357
and created the Negro Exhibit,

00:09:35.381 --> 00:09:37.292
including Du Bois,

00:09:37.316 --> 00:09:39.920
came to Buffalo,
four years after the fair,

00:09:39.944 --> 00:09:42.135
to start the Niagara Movement,

00:09:42.159 --> 00:09:45.506
which set the groundwork
for the creation of the NAACP.

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:47.212
AYGTK: It's not just black folks

00:09:47.236 --> 00:09:50.030
who had a peculiar experience
at the 1901 fair.

00:09:50.403 --> 00:09:53.310
An official handbook informed fair-goers:

00:09:53.334 --> 00:09:55.349
MJ: "Please remember:"

00:09:55.373 --> 00:09:57.348
JMR: "... once you get inside the gate,"

00:09:57.372 --> 00:10:00.166
AYGTK: "... you are a part of the show."